# Analytical shipment costs
BudgetCostFeature=Include shipments in costs
BudgetCostFeatureDescription=Values shipped products not covered by supplier invoices. Analytical calculation only, without additional accounting entries or stock movements.
BudgetCostFormulaHelp=Retained cost = invoiced purchases + uncovered shipments + remaining supplier commitments. Example: 12 ordered, 10 shipped and 4 invoiced units give 4 at invoice cost, 6 at shipment cost and 2 at order cost. Matching uses project, product and unit, respecting invoice allocations.
BudgetCostChronologyHelp=Amounts are movements within the period; earlier history is used for matching. A shipment valued at 100 in March, invoiced at 120 in April, contributes 100 in March and +20 in April. Adjustments may be negative.
BudgetCostQuantityHelp=Quantities accumulate through the period end. Invoices cover the oldest shipments without using any quantity twice. Currently valid documents are authoritative: backdated corrections may change an earlier report.
BudgetCostPriceHelp=Latest tariff: the most recently recorded unit supplier price excluding tax, after discounts, on or before the shipment date, across authorized suppliers. Missing shipment dates use the validation date. Future dates are capped at validation. WAC is read in the shipment entity at validation (Stock module required).
BudgetCostHistoryHelp=Both available prices are captured at validation; changing the method recalculates reports from these snapshots. Unprovable historical values remain unvalued: current prices never replace them. Snapshots and settings survive deactivation. Direct database changes or imports without native events are not a reliable history.
